✔ [Phase 1 - Discovery and Contracts] Define dynamic bottom-panel targeting and DF binding resolution contracts. @done(26-07-31 12:00)
    ✔ Confirm target focus and overlay lifecycle for fortress mode (`dwarfmode/Default`). @done(26-07-31 12:00)
    ✔ Identify all bottom-panel ui-menu buttons that need labels (citizen, etc.) and define one stable semantic ID per button. @done(26-07-31 12:00)
    ✔ Design a dynamic bounds sampler that re-queries button rectangles from native UI tiles and invalidates cache on size/layout changes. @done(26-07-31 12:00)
    ✔ Design a binding resolver that reads the active keybinding from DF for each semantic button ID. @done(26-07-31 12:00)
    ✔ Define failure behavior: if bounds or binding are unavailable for one button, suppress only that button label. @done(26-07-31 12:00)
    Decisions:
    - Focus/lifecycle contract: render only while `dwarfmode/Default` is active; clear all cached geometry and labels immediately when focus leaves the screen.
    - Semantic-ID contract: each label target is keyed by a stable semantic menu ID (for example `citizens`) that is independent of on-screen position and current hotkey text.
    - Button-catalog contract: the model owns the complete bottom-panel button catalog and maps each semantic ID to one DF action binding key; overlay code consumes snapshots only.
    - Geometry contract: bounds are dynamically sampled from live native tiles, cached per layout signature, and invalidated on screen-size changes or panel-layout shifts.
    - Binding contract: hotkey text is resolved from active DF bindings every refresh cycle from the semantic ID's mapped action; no hardcoded label fallback is permitted.
    - Failure contract: labels are suppressed per button when either bounds or active binding data is unavailable; other button labels remain visible.
    - Rendering contract: each label anchor is derived from the sampled bounding box (corner + inset), not fixed coordinates.
    Docs:
    - README.md (module, overlay, and reload conventions)
    - Docs/hover-action-rail-proposal.md (target/anchor ownership patterns and dynamic placement ideas)
    - https://docs.dfhack.org/en/stable/docs/dev/Lua%20API.html (DFHack Lua API reference)

